{"id": "EUVD-2026-103691", "enisaUuid": "fe4cfab0-becf-3155-a5e5-9c62bd0ca286", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: use finish_no_open() for non-regular inodes\n\nAn O_CREAT open can find an existing symlink or another non-regular\ninode. cifs_atomic_open() calls finish_open() on it and attaches a\ncifsFileInfo. Symlink inodes have no CIFS release operation, so the\ndentry reference held by cifsFileInfo is leaked. FMODE_OPENED also\nprevents the VFS from following the symlink.\n\nTrack whether cifs_do_create() returned an open server handle. For\nnon-regular inodes, close the handle if present, remove the pending\nopen, and call finish_no_open() so the VFS can continue the lookup.\nDo not set FMODE_CREATED unless a regular file was opened. For\nO_NOFOLLOW with __O_REGULAR, return -ELOOP before the VFS's\n-EFTYPE check.\n\nDefer closing a legacy POSIX handle on a non-regular inode until\nafter inode lookup. This avoids closing it again if lookup fails.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/045532f920d86dd76600b635f9756e5fd671ddfc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed03d547598c92a036f20e89156540995cac889a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70a7918fda54a06d836acc91eb9a3c7e860fe0a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c07deb26273155c180aedfd9041ab58015d2521", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e66cf1625ec4a3fe68346119f371def713fd0a4d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98451", "GHSA-8vx8-gc8p-9x99"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20483108-11a5-316c-9c57-d9936003bafc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "23a4cb8d-9a80-3bb7-a598-5ca481740a96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.6"}, {"id": "30ba00fa-8515-309a-b9d2-c7c26c70f599", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "41ef57d1-c4b1-373a-81f0-7456091d7160", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d2c127197dfc0b2bae62a52e1e0d3e3ff493919e <e66cf1625ec4a3fe68346119f371def713fd0a4d"}, {"id": "54c50a49-68ae-3933-887d-d7da4853fb66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5542d3bd-13c9-3cd5-b5b8-c90d23cf7900", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "57a622ce-e3bb-3b79-b2ca-5daff2b9b412", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d2c127197dfc0b2bae62a52e1e0d3e3ff493919e <70a7918fda54a06d836acc91eb9a3c7e860fe0a0"}, {"id": "8d05f615-d243-35d7-b563-33c6b53d5fdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d2c127197dfc0b2bae62a52e1e0d3e3ff493919e <3c07deb26273155c180aedfd9041ab58015d2521"}, {"id": "8e33e0f8-21b4-3fe1-aad7-8e33f83b610a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a0b68337-b21b-3d15-bbb6-b72cb9703323", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d2c127197dfc0b2bae62a52e1e0d3e3ff493919e <045532f920d86dd76600b635f9756e5fd671ddfc"}, {"id": "c9f207f3-b595-3752-b45f-c5a7cf56aa9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d2c127197dfc0b2bae62a52e1e0d3e3ff493919e <ed03d547598c92a036f20e89156540995cac889a"}, {"id": "f0c13ab8-92b5-3ac4-a470-da6243665178", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c8c1cc98-f522-3cdf-8963-54f2bb0a3e74", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}